# TODO — MiniDB

Updated: 2026-10-17 · branch `dev` (in sync with `origin/dev`)
Full detail lives in `notes/` (start at `ainotes.md`). This file is the short, actionable list.

## Bugs to fix

- [ ] **DAP "port error" on the second laptop.** Starting the debugger errors out. Cause is
      almost certainly a legacy `type = "executable"` codelldb adapter there — nvim-dap only
      substitutes `${port}` for `type = "server"`, so codelldb receives the literal `${port}`.
      Fix: run `scripts/setup-nvim-dap.sh` (step 3 now moves such files aside), `:Lazy sync`,
      restart. Checks + error capture: `notes/23-debug-lazyvim-troubleshoot.md`. The primary
      machine is verified clean.
- [ ] **Tokenizer silently drops unknown chars** (`, ; ( ) = < >` and digits). It no longer
      hangs (stopgap), but they produce no token and no error. Needs real tokens / error
      reporting. `notes/41-tokenizer-state.md` defect 7.
- [ ] **`tokenize` ignores `list_push`'s return value** (the word push *and* the `*` push). A
      grow failure goes unnoticed. defect 2.
- [ ] **`grow_list_capisity` returns `void`**; failure surfaces only through the sticky
      `had_error` side effect. defect 3.
- [ ] **`had_error` is overloaded + sticky** — cannot distinguish "malformed SQL" from "out of
      memory". defect 4.
- [ ] **`token_type_name` is not implemented** (header declaration commented out). The 27-case
      body is recoverable from `tests/scratch.c` (`scratch_type_name`).
      `notes/42-token-type-name.md`.
- [ ] **EOF token fields are inconsistent**: `input_string` = start of input, `start_index` =
      end. Natural value is `lexer.input_string + lexer.cursor_position`. defect 6.

## Next up — tokenizer (in order)

- [ ] **Keyword table.** Only `"select"` is a keyword; add the other 10
      (`FROM, WHERE, INSERT, INTO, VALUES, CREATE, TABLE, DELETE, UPDATE, SET`) as a `static
      const` table in `tokenizer.c` (not the header), matched with `strncasecmp` **plus** the
      length check. Test case-insensitivity (`select`, `SeLeCt`).
- [ ] **Punctuation/operators as real tokens:** `,` `;` `(` `)` first, then `=` `!=` `<` `<=`
      `>` `>=`. Generalise the hand-rolled `*` branch into a small `switch`/table on `peek`.
- [ ] **Numbers and strings** (quotes excluded; unterminated string → `had_error`).
- [ ] **Implement `token_type_name`** (see bug above).
- [ ] **Guide checklist tests** (~line 2610): position checks; prefix cases
      `"selection"`/`"SEL"`/`"SE"`/`"S"` → `TOKEN_IDENT`; `"SELECT@"` → error naming the
      character; identifiers with digits/underscores (`user_id2`) but not starting with a digit;
      `token_list_free(NULL)` safe; 10,000-token stress input.

## Open design decisions (decide before the parser grows)

- [ ] **OOM reporting:** should `tokenize` return `NULL`, or the list with `had_error = true`?
      If `NULL`, the caller has no list to read `had_error` from.
- [ ] **`token_type_name` spelling:** enum names (`"STAR"`, `"LTE"`) vs user-facing SQL symbols
      (`"*"`, `"<="`). The guide derives `expect()` messages from it, so decide now.
- [ ] **EOF token field convention** (see bug above).

